# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Production build
build/
dist/

# Environment variables (secret keys)
.env
.env.local

# Debug logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# System files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
```.

### Why This is Important
By listing `node_modules/` in this file, Git will automatically ignore that folder. This allows you to push your code to GitHub **without** the massive dependencies folder, keeping your repository small and fast. When you clone it on your home laptop, you simply run `npm install` to get those files back.
